    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's the same program from the previous page:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "c",
      "content": "1#include <stdio.h>\n2\n3int main() {\n4\n5    double total;\n6    int result;\n7\n8    printf(\"Enter total: \");\n9    scanf(\"%lf\", &total);\n10  \n11    // Check if total is greater than 100\n12    result = total > 100;\n13\n14    printf(\"%d\", result);\n15\n16    return 0;\n17}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, > is the greater than operator that's comparing the total with 100 (total > 100)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This expression total > 100 evaluates to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "1 if the condition is met (total is greater than 100).",
        "0 if the condition is not met (total is 100 or less)."
      ]
    },
